Stephanie Christian fresh off her  quarantine she thought she was exposed  she's okay she is the White House press  secretary communications director  Stephanie glad you're okay quick  question for you how how much detail  does the president know about the 1,000  page bill that Steve minuchin guarantees  he'll sign the president has been kept  in form simunition has been on the phone  with him constantly the president has  been very active in this process so he's  well aware of what is in it he's been  pushing for Congress to do the right  thing and get ready to help the American  people so we're really looking forward  to this vote today so that he can sign  it into law well that's good news  Stephanie yesterday when we were talking  about what was going on on Capitol Hill  and we heard this about this bill that  Nancy Pelosi had been talking about the  one Brian's talking about a thousand  pages long and people saw all these  things that had nothing to do with kovat  you know Kennedy Center funding and  student debt loan debt forgiveness and  airline emission standards and stuff  like that when you looked at that at the  White House what was the point of view  of the president regarding that because  it had little to do with the disaster  that's going on right now you know it  was disappointing it was a disappointing  thing that they would try to sneak some  things in there when when this is right  now the focus it's all hands on deck  truly and the focus is to to get money  to the American people to get you know  loans to small businesses I was very  very disappointing but again I'm glad  that they were able to work so late into  the evening and looks like we're gonna  have something good and we're gonna be  able to take care of the people of this  country so yesterday you know well every  day the president's had this briefing  Andrew Cuomo the governor of New York  has had a briefing and yesterday this is  what the governor of New York said we  need the federal help and we need the  federal help now different regions have  different curves of the infection New  York is the canary in the coal mine New  York is going first we have the highest  and the fastest rate of infection what  happens to New York  is going to wind up happening to  California and Washington State and  Illinois it's just a matter of time so  Stephanie what's going on between  Governor Cuomo set the record straight  the president's tweeting saying that  they're friends but Cuomo said he needs  30,000 ventilators I know that the Vice  President sent two thousand or the  president in the task force sent 2,000  yesterday they're gonna send two  thousand today but then Governor Cuomo  says will you pick the 26,000 that will  die  what's your response I did hear him say  that and you know New York is the  epicenter right now that is absolutely  the truth but the president has put FEMA  now in charge and they are working to  get supplies to all of the hardest hit  areas New York is certainly going to be  one of them New York is certainly a  priority for this president because it's  one of the hardest hit areas we're  working day and night I've got to say  that with the president's leadership the  Vice President in the task force have  truly been working around the clock to  do everything they can so supplies are  going to start really moving quickly I  would also like to point out that we've  done more tests in the last eight days  then South Korea was able to do in in  eight weeks in South Korea was the gold  standard remember so the president the  task force again working around the  clock I've been watching my colleagues  work day and night to get everything  they can to every state and we're really  we're really looking up and it's gonna  be on the upswing  Stephanie how real is this Easter day  and how well-informed was the rest of  the task force that the president was  going to say that yesterday that his  goal was to open up by Easter you know I  don't know how well inform they were I  think that the president as he has been  doing is very hopeful and wants to have  a message of hope to the American people  I think he would love it if we were  opened up for business yesterday but  after the 15 days when we see the data  come in we'll see where we're at and I  think the president will make his  decision now but he is hopeful and I  will tell you something for as somebody  who was just in quarantine for two weeks  it's tough it's tough and I imagine a  lot of people want to try to get out  there and get back to work as long as  there's social distancing so we'll see  what happens once the 15 days goes past  and we've got new data sets the  president listens to his medical team he  listens  - dr. Burks dr. pouchy he listens to his  task force so I think they'll make some  recommendations and then he'll make  ultimately the final decision right and  dr. foul she said yesterday at the  briefing he said that that particular  time line was aspirational and  flexibility was needed but as you know  Stephanie a couple of days ago  ambassador birx was there and doctor  foul she was not members of the media  went a little crazy like hey wait a  minute you know he said some things he  kind of brushed back at the president  when the president was talking about the  hopeful drug trials is something going  on doctor foul she was asked on you know  what they're trying to do in some  programs and the media and pundits and  stuff like that earlier on mornings on  the mall which is on the radio down  there in Washington listen that is  really unfortunate I would wish that  that would stop because we have a much  bigger problem here than trying to point  out differences they're really  fundamentally at the core when you look  at things there are not differences the  president has listened to what I have  said and what the other people on the  task force have said when I've made  recommendations he's taken them he's  never counted all over written me the  idea of just pitting one against the  other is just not helpful I wish that  would stop what we'd look ahead at the  challenge we have to pull together to  get over this thing  Stephanie why why are there people who  are trying to create a rift or is it as  simple as he's not here today what's  going on you know it's it's more of the  same I think a lot of the media are  wasting an opportunity to get facts out  to the American people that is the  responsibility of the media and right  now it's more vital than ever that they  are trying to do that unfortunately once  again some members of the media are  using a really important time in our  country to try and and divide people on  the task force I couldn't agree with dr.  foul chief more I've sat in meetings  with them the president listens to his  team doctor foul she lays out  recommendations the president asks  questions and he listens to his team  they are in lockstep together he listens  to all of them so it's unfortunate what  the media is doing and I've been I've  been saying all along please use this  time to get factual information to the  American people because I don't think  people at home care if dr. Fuji and the  president get along which they do and  just because sometimes people aren't  there they're out doing work they have a  lot of work to do so we're rotating  people in and out from the task force  Stephanie we're glad to see you back at  work glad that you tested negative thank  you two weeks right yeah two weeks that  was wrong I've got to tell you I feel  great I feel great I'm so grateful to  the doctors who helped take care of me  the president was absolutely supportive  of this but I cannot wait to get back in  that White House and and help out oh  that's great because so many people have  said did you do anything there the  silver lining is we are home with our  families but I guess for you you're so  busy I thought maybe a break would allow  you to take a pause and breathe but I'm  sure you were working from home no yes I  was definitely working from home but  you're kind of blinded you don't you're  not there so it was frustrating I'm very  excited to get to the White House all  right all right Stephanie good luck to  you thank you very much for joining us  we need to get a busy day

